//============================================================================
// nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads --- Calibre DRC wrapper deck   (PROJECT-OWNED)
//
// Run it with:   ASIC/genus-innovus/scripts/calibre/run_drc.sh
// or by hand:    cd <rundir> && DRC_GDS=/abs/path/to.gds \
//                calibre -drc -hier -turbo 8 -nowait <this file>
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
// --------------------
// The TSMC deck /tsmc65pdk/.../CLN65S_9M_6X1Z1U.26_2a ships with *placeholder*
// specification statements that the customer is expected to replace:
//
//     LAYOUT PATH    "GDSFILENAME"          <- literal string, not a variable
//     LAYOUT PRIMARY "TOPCELLNAME"          <- literal string, not a variable
//     DRC RESULTS DATABASE "DRC_RES.db"
//     DRC SUMMARY REPORT   "DRC.rep"
//
// Pointing Calibre straight at the foundry deck therefore fails with
//     Failure to open input file GDSFILENAME for read access.
// because Calibre looks for a file *named* "GDSFILENAME" in the current
// directory. It is not a variable and nothing in Innovus, Tcl or the shell
// substitutes it. (`set GDSFILENAME ...` in a Tcl script sets a *Tcl*
// variable and has no effect whatsoever on the SVRF deck.)
//
// THE LOAD-BEARING LINE IS `DRC ICSTATION YES` -- DO NOT REMOVE IT
// ---------------------------------------------------------------
// SVRF normally rejects a specification statement that is given twice:
//     ERROR: Error SPC1 on line N of <deck> -
//            superfluous specification statement: layout primary.
// so simply setting LAYOUT PRIMARY here and then INCLUDEing the foundry deck
// (which sets it again) is a hard error -- verified on this site, both
// orderings, with and without -turbo.
//
// `DRC ICSTATION YES` switches Calibre into the mode Calibre Interactive uses:
// duplicate specification statements are tolerated and the ones in the
// TOP-LEVEL rule file win. That is what makes this wrapper pattern legal.
// Verified 2026-08-06 on Calibre v2023.1_18.8: removing this one line turns a
// clean run back into SPC1.
//
// Everything below the INCLUDE is the unmodified foundry deck. The foundry
// deck is READ-ONLY (/tsmc65pdk is shared, lab-wide collateral) and is not
// copied, patched or sed-ed by this flow.
//============================================================================

// ---- must come first: enables top-level override of the deck's placeholders
DRC ICSTATION YES

// ---- input layout -----------------------------------------------------------
// $DRC_GDS is expanded by Calibre itself. SVRF expands environment variables in
// *file path* strings (LAYOUT PATH, INCLUDE, DRC RESULTS DATABASE) but NOT in
// cell-name strings -- so LAYOUT PRIMARY below must stay literal. Verified.
LAYOUT PATH    "$DRC_GDS"
LAYOUT SYSTEM  GDSII
LAYOUT PRIMARY "nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads"

// ---- outputs (relative -> they land in whatever directory you run from) -----
DRC RESULTS DATABASE "nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads.drc.results" ASCII
DRC SUMMARY REPORT   "nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads.drc.summary" REPLACE HIER
DRC CELL NAME YES CELL SPACE XFORM

// Cap results per check. A first full-chip run on a design that has never been
// through signoff DRC can generate millions of results (density and sealring
// checks especially) and an unbounded ASCII database will fill the disk.
// Raise to ALL only once the count is known to be sane.
DRC MAXIMUM RESULTS 1000
DRC MAXIMUM VERTEX  4096

// ---- process option: WE ARE LP, AND THE DECK DOES NOT ASSUME IT --------------
// The foundry deck's `#DEFINE LP` is COMMENTED OUT in the shipped file, and the
// deck never defines it itself. Without it the deck checks the wrong DPO.W.1 /
// DPO.S.1/2/3 variants (deck :9008-9014 UNSELECTs the general forms and
// substitutes the `.A` forms only under #IFDEF LP) and skips the N65LP HVD_N
// block at :10446 entirely. This design is CLN65LP throughout - tcbn65lp std
// cells, tphn65lpgv2od3_sl IO. Defining it HERE, before the INCLUDE, is legal
// and leaves the read-only foundry deck untouched.
#DEFINE LP

// ---- the foundry deck, unmodified -------------------------------------------
// 9-metal 6X1Z1U stack, matching the Innovus GdsOutMap used by write_stream
// (PRTF_EDI_N65_gdsout_6X1Z1U.24a.map). Kept literal on purpose: the metal
// option is fixed for this tapeout and a silently-wrong deck is worse than an
// edit. If the metal stack ever changes, change this line AND the map file
// passed to write_stream together.
//
// NOT FIXABLE FROM HERE: the deck also has `#DEFINE WLCSP_SEALRING` active at
// its line 62, and we are WIRE BOND. That selects SR_EDGE = CHIP_WISR NOT
// SCORE_WLCSP (:3501) rather than the wire-bond branch (:3503), so the CSR.*
// corner geometry may be derived from degenerate inputs. SVRF has no
// #UNDEFINE, so undoing it needs a project copy of the deck header - do that
// only once the broker has confirmed their own switch set.
INCLUDE "/tsmc65pdk/65/CMOS/util/MAIN_DRC_TopMu/CLN65S_9M_6X1Z1U.26_2a"
